blockage_sweep.json", "PYTHONPATH=src python -m pytest tests/test_ibm_epsilon_gram.py tests/test_ibm_epsilon_gram_solver_smoke.py -q -> 12 passed", "PYTHONPATH=src python /root/tp-agent/work/m18209/audit_m18209/verify_m18141.py -> audit_m18209/verify_m18141.json"], "external_anchor": ["joconnor22/LIFE @ 2af2428: inc/Utils.h:220-231 diracDelta, src/IBMNode.cpp:73-74 spread, :140-180 support, :186-205 computeDs, src/Objects.cpp:235-320 computeEpsilon (A[i,j]=sum_s w_i(s) w_j(s) ds_j, solve A*eps=1), :271-272 recompute cadence - transplanted line by line", "OSS binary NOT built or executed by the delivery (Boost/LAPACK + full FSI case), disclosed in predeclared.json.baseline_control.oss_note and REPORT section 7/8 => no program-vs-program comparison exists", "physics reference: 2-D unbounded cylinder Cd band 1.30-1.40 at Re=100 (Braza 1986 / Norberg 1993) as cited in run_xval.py:70 LIT_CD_BAND"], "declared_level": 3, "verdict_basis": "L1 met (analytic delta identities + 12 passing tests). L2 met (506-line real implementation: markers+ds -> Gram solve -> corrected spread -> interpolated force, loop/vectorised/IBMStencil three paths agreeing to 0.0-2.2e-16; an independent auditor re-implementation reproduces A2 2.4548e-02, deposit cost 8.5217e-01, eps 1.8116-1.8796). L3 met: the correction is not a parallel code path - it rides the repo's IBMStencil.spread (ibm_force_transfer.py:126) and is exercised through collide_bgk/stream/body_source_2d/disc_mask_2d in a passing solver-loop smoke test, with bit-identical agreement between the stencil path and the loop reference. L4 WITHHELD: (a) 0 registered rows in tensor_benchmark_cases for the anchor -> no platform referee/tolerance; (b) the only independent physical KPI fails the 15% standard: Cd(Re=100)=1.6156 vs band centre 1.35 = +19.7% (honest FAIL, declared by the report); (c) the machine-precision PASS rows are true by construction - the Gram system A*eps=1 makes constant-field spread->interp exact identically (audit residual A*eps-1 = 3.3e-16), so they certify wiring, not fidelity; the non-constant-field residual 2.19e-3 is the only non-tautological identity row and it is not grid/time converged; (d) the physics mean carries a 0.4-shedding-period window (std 1.39, ~+-2%). L5 not claimed (no experimental anchor, no new physical capability - a normalisation fix).", "findings": [{"id": "F1", "sev": "moderate", "what": "predeclared H1 conjunction is falsified and never adjudicated: H1 required A1 round-trip < 1e-6 AND A1 total-force conservation < 1e-6; measured conservation deviation is 2.517e-02 (N=16) and 8.522e-01 (N=32), and predeclared H0's own falsifier ('conservation >= 15%') fires at N=32. The report reports both numbers (section 4.2) and the trade-off, but then substitutes the round-trip KPI as the acceptance basis ('方法验收依据仍是 section 4.1') - a post-hoc KPI switch, not a predeclared adjudication. No fabrication; framing defect."}, {"id": "F2", "sev": "moderate", "what": "no registered referee: tensor_benchmark_cases has 0 rows for the anchor, so no case/tolerance exists to machine-adjudicate; benchmark.json is the delivery's own artefact (audit rebuilt 4 of its rows independently and they agree to 15 digits)."}, {"id": "F3", "sev": "moderate", "what": "headline '210x - 1e14 improvement' rows are tautological: A*eps=1 forces constant-field reproduction, so the N=16/N=32 machine-zero round-trip is a property of the construction (audit residual 3.3e-16), not an empirical finding. Disclosed in section 4.2's mechanism sentence but presented as validation in section 4.1/8; the substantive numbers are the A2 control (2.5e-2/4.6e-1) and the deposit cost."}, {"id": "F4", "sev": "moderate", "what": "the blockage falsification rests on two points measured with different temporal-averaging protocols: main point n_steps 700 / n_transient 500 / n_avg 200, sweep point 700 / 300 / 400 (blockage_sweep.json). The report says the only changed variable is the box, but the averaging window changed too, and n_avg 200 is ~0.4 shedding periods - so 'blockage does not explain +20%' is confounded by statistics, and the two-point fit (k=-0.09) is admitted to be meaningless."}, {"id": "F5", "sev": "minor", "what": "'三臂互相差 <=3.9%' is normalised against the largest arm; max pairwise spread is (1.6817-1.6156)/1.6156 = 4.09%. Same for 'A1 vs A2 0.9%' (0.91%, correct)."}, {"id": "F6", "sev": "minor", "what": "fig4_convergence.png caption claims the running mean 'is flat to a few percent ... converged within the stated spread' while the report's own section 5 states the 200-step window is ~0.4 shedding periods with std 1.39 (~+-2%); the figure name/caption overstates convergence."}, {"id": "F7", "sev": "minor", "what": "traceability nits: predeclared.json stamps mission_id=17862 (not 18141, the restore+verify mission); benchmark.json/results.json provenance git_sha=0a1cf0e2 is the parent of the delivery commit e2743f0e with git_dirty=true, so an auditor must walk the tree to bind artefacts to the delivered module (audit did: no source drift, the module is byte-identical to what the numbers came from)."}, {"id": "F8", "sev": "positive", "what": "discipline that held: honest FAIL declared for the physics arm instead of retuning; a control arm with an identical kernel isolates the single changed variable (epsilon); predeclared thresholds frozen and published; every artefact sha256-listed in manifest.json; tests assert invariants (partition of unity, no periodic wrap, stencil-vs-loop identity 0.0), not just execution."}], "checks_run": ["pytest 12/12 (26.18 s), module selftest via python -m, run_xval.py Part A 8/8 arms + Part B A1 rerun, sweep_blockage.py 192x96 rerun, auditor's independent re-implementation of support/spread/interp, Gram-residual probe (A*eps-1), 3 t_design / tensor_benchmark_cases referee query"], "checks_not_run": ["OSS LIFE binary never built/executed (Boost+LAPACK+FSI needed) -> no program-vs-program comparison; the anchor is a line-cited semantics transplant", "3-D path, flexible-body per-step epsilon recompute, MPI decomposition: out of scope, declared unimplemented", "no grid/time-step convergence study of the identity arms (single-shot by predeclared design)", "no longer averaging window / finer D for the cylinder arm (the predeclared improvement path, not executed)", "no cluster rerun (all numbers reproduced locally on the same loongarch64 box)"], "independence_limits": "The auditor shares the host, torch build and OSS reading with the delivery; independence is in the code path (auditor re-implemented support/spread/interp from the LIFE formulas, did not call run_xval.py) and in the referee (rebuilt 4 benchmark rows). No third-party executable reference was available, so 'fidelity' beyond the analytic identities is NOT independently established - only reproducibility is.", "path_note": "All paths are absolute into the audited worktree /root/tp-agent/work/m18141 (mission 18141, HEAD e2743f0e; repo-relative equivalents src/tensorlbm/ibm_epsilon_gram.py, tests/test_ibm_epsilon_gram*.py, xval/XVAL-LBM-IBM-EPSILON-GRAM-IMPLICIT-CORRECTION/*). Audit artefacts ship in this branch: audit_m18209/*, verdict_m18209.sql.", "disposition": "approve with notes (L3 confirmed, L4 withheld): the capability is real, reproducible and integrated; carry F1 (predeclared H1/H0 adjudication) and F4 (confounded blockage inference) into the ledger as open items, and keep the physics arm as honest-FAIL rather than a pass.", "audit_artifacts": ["audit_m18209/verify_m18141.py (independent re-derivation script)", "audit_m18209/verify_m18141.json (its output, cross-checked against benchmark.json)", "audit_m18209/AUDIT_M18141.md (severity-ranked findings, checks run/not run, disposition)", "audit_m18209/fig_audit_m18141.png (audit evidence figure)"]}$json$::jsonb,
